    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Embraced in 1760 by the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} Pontifex Eve Cavanant, who recognized her exceptional intellect, Luna Demian devoted herself to cloistered magical research rather than clan politics &mdash; a choice that advanced her scholarship but left her powerless to avoid an unwanted reassignment to San Francisco as Regent. She transferred her resentment over that reassignment onto the Kuei-jin, and it was Demian who developed the Ward Versus Cathayans ritual that the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla} used to seal off the Cathayan Free Zone.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Demian has little patience for social niceties, preferring to conduct research on captured Kuei-jin subjects, and is chillingly polite when interrupted. Paranoid since her transfer, she surrounds herself with five to twelve armed ghoul decoys dressed in her exact likeness, coordinated by two-way radio at the suggestion of her prot\u00e9g\u00e9 Martin Franckel.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Eve Cavanant. Prot\u00e9g\u00e9: Martin Franckel. Disciplines (as printed): Auspex 5, Celerity 2, Dominate 5, Fortitude 4, Obfuscate 3, Presence 1, Serpentis 1, Thaumaturgy 5 (Path of Blood 5, Path of Shadowcrafting 5, Lure of Flames 3, Hands of Destruction 3, Path of the Levinbolt 5, Spirit Manipulation 2). Rituals include the Ward Versus Cathayans, known otherwise only to Franckel and the Las Vegas Chantry.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
